    "content": "NovaMind Assistant handles the core automation tasks\u2014solid execution, reasonable pricing tier. But here's the catch: support is fragmented. Ticket got shuffled between three different teams before getting any real traction. That's a workflow killer when you're integrating this into production systems. Feature-wise, does what it claims. Value proposition holds up if you're doing straightforward automation. Just factor in extra time for issue resolution. Worth evaluating if support ops improve."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 309,
    "day": 168,
    "content": "ugh okay so real talk\u2014nms assistant has saved me HOURS on my content workflow but WHY is support acting like i'm playing hot potato with my ticket?? \ud83e\udd14 been bounced between 3 different teams in a week and nobody's actually helping. love the product itself (the writing suggestions are legit) but the support experience is genuinely frustrating rn \ud83d\ude24\n\nlike i get it, you're growing, but come on... my problem isn't that complicated #SaaS #NovaMind #SupportMatters"
  },
  {
    "post_id": 310,
    "day": 168,
    "content": "just spent 2 hrs on a gig that would've taken me 4+ before nova. the new summarization thing actually... works? like it's not perfect but cutting my prep time in half is lowkey a game changer for side hustles \ud83d\udcaa still wish the pricing was more flexible but can't complain when i'm shipping faster #NovaWin #GigEconomy"
  },
  {
    "post_id": 311,
    "day": 168,
    "content": "yo so been using NovaMind Assistant to manage my store's social posts and inventory labels and like... it's doing the job? \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2640\ufe0f the interface got a little clunkier after the last update tho ngl. takes me an extra minute or two to find what i need now. not a dealbreaker but kinda wish they'd kept it simpler lol\n\nthe AI writing suggestions are still solid when they work. just inconsistent some days??? one minute it's nailing my vibe, next day it feels like a bot wrote a generic essay \ud83d\ude05\n\ndef worth the cost if you're drowning in content tasks like me, but honestly wouldn't recommend it if you're on a tight budget. there's cheaper options out there doing similar stuff. NovaMind's just... fine, ya know? not life-changing but not a waste either #NovaMindAssistant #RetailLife #SmallBizTools"
  },
  {
    "post_id": 312,
    "day": 168,
    "content": "ngl been using NovaMind for a few weeks and it's *fast* \u2014 like genuinely snappy compared to what i was using before \ud83d\ude80 but here's the thing... filed a bug report like 10 days ago about some performance issues and literally haven't heard back? it's just sitting there in the void \ud83d\ude05 \n\nlove the speed when things work, hate the silence when they don't. kinda defeats the purpose if support just ghosts you know? \n\n#NovaMindAssistant #SaaS #TechSupport"
  },
  {
    "post_id": 313,
